Please generate me a basic SVG for a technical talk that visualizes the slide
"What does a VMM need to create a VM?" (see 03-background.md), similar in style
to from-host-vmm-process-to-vm-guest.svg. Keep it simple, high-level and
approachable:

- The VMM provides virtual devices, e.g. two virtual disks (disk 1, disk 2)
- The guest sees them as normal disks (/dev/vda, /dev/vdb) and writes to them
  as usual; keep it free of PCI/NVMe details - high level, not technical
- Every access to a disk is trapped by KVM and forwarded back to the VMM
- The VMM implements the devices and does the real work, e.g. writing into
  disk1.img / disk2.img on the host
- Take-away: virtual hardware is just software in the VMM
